{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-395867-r4531800","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Murgh Musallam (Indian Stewed Spiced Chicken)","sourcePageId":395867,"sourceRevision":"4531800","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-08-21T00:55:19Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Murgh%20Musallam%20(Indian%20Stewed%20Spiced%20Chicken)&oldid=4531800","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:09:19.205Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Indian recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for curry","Category:Recipes using almond","Category:Recipes using cardamom","Category:Recipes using cashew","Category:Recipes using chicken","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using cinnamon stick","Category:Recipes using clove","Category:Recipes using coriander","Category:Recipes using cumin","Category:Recipes using ginger-garlic paste","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using mint","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"f91dfe2399d4d99f0c99aa6cc2c45aee75334f628bc601be8253a6444dc49572","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Curry recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}{{Recipe}}\n== Ingredients ==\n\n=== Chicken ===\n\n* 600 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Ginger Garlic Paste|ginger-garlic paste]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]] juice\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] red [[Cookbook:Chiles|chile]] powder\n* ¼ tsp [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]] powder\n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Turmeric|turmeric]] powder\n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n\n=== Spice blend ===\n\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]] seeds\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]] seeds\n* 2-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] piece [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* 2 green [[Cookbook:Cardamom|cardamom]] pods\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]]\n* ¼ tsp [[Cookbook:Grater|grated]] [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]] (jayaphala)\n* 1 medium [[Cookbook:Mace|mace]] javitri\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cardamom|black cardamom]] (moti elachi)\n\n=== Curry ===\n\n* 8 [[Cookbook:Almond|almonds]]\n* 10 [[Cookbook:Cashew|cashews]] or 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Poppy Seed|poppy seeds]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] (2 [[Cookbook:Each|ea]].) [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]] \n* 1 large [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomato]], puréed\n* 4 slit green [[Cookbook:Chiles|chiles]]\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Oil and Fat|oil]] or [[Cookbook:Clarified Butter|ghee]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Ginger Garlic Paste|ginger-garlic paste]]\n* 1 tsp red chile powder (use more if required)\n* 2 tbsp chopped [[Cookbook:Mint|mint]] leaves\n* 2–3 cups water\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n=== Chicken ===\n\n# Cut chicken into bite-sized pieces and wash well.\n# [[Cookbook:Marinating|Marinate]] chicken with remaining ingredients for 1–4 hours.\n\n=== Spice blend ===\n\n# Dry [[Cookbook:Roasting|roast]] all the ingredients until light brown and aromatic.\n# Allow to cool then grind into a coarse powder.\n\n=== Curry ===\n\n# Soak almonds and cashews in water for 10–15 minutes. Peel almonds.\n# Grind the almonds and cashews into a smooth paste, adding 1–2 tbsp water if required.\n# Heat 2–3 tsp oil in a [[Cookbook:Skillet|pan]] or [[Cookbook:Wok|wok]]. Add chopped onion, and [[Cookbook:Sautéing|sauté]] until golden brown. Allow to cool, then grind into a paste, trying not to add water.\n# Heat oil or ghee in a pan or wok. Add onion paste, green chili, and ginger-garlic paste, then sauté until onion paste leaves oil.\n# Add marinated chicken pieces, and mix well. Cover and cook for 5–6 minutes over medium-low heat, stirring occasionally.\n# Mix in the red chili powder, prepared spice blend, and tomato puree. Cover and cook, stirring occasionally, until oil starts to floats on the surface.\n# Add water, and cook for 3–4 minutes over medium heat.\n# Mix in the nut paste, mint, and salt. Cook until gravy becomes thick and oil starts to float.\n# Remove from the heat, and stir in the coriander leaves.\n\n[[Category:Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken]]\n[[Category:Recipes for curry]]\n[[Category:Recipes using almond]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cardamom]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cashew]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cinnamon stick]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ginger-garlic paste]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mint]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Murgh Musallam (Indian Stewed Spiced Chicken)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"600 g chicken","sourceText":"600 g chicken","amountText":"600 g chicken","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste","sourceText":"1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste","amountText":"1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 tbsp lemon juice","sourceTex